# SmartFare — Smart Vehicle Fare System

A console-based C++ application that simulates a multi-vehicle fare/booking system (think a simplified Uber/Ola backend). It demonstrates core OOP concepts — inheritance, polymorphism, operator overloading, friend functions, static members, exceptions, and lambdas — inside a single working CLI program.

## Features

- **7 vehicle types**, each with its own fare slab logic, via runtime polymorphism:
  - Car, Bus, Bike, Auto, Luxury Car, Truck, Shared Cab
- **Customer accounts** with types (`regular`, `student`, `senior`, `member`), each carrying its own discount rate
- **Coupon codes**: `SAVE10`, `FIRST50`, `VIT25` (total discount capped at 50%)
- **Extra charges**: night surcharge, peak-hour surcharge, waiting-time charge, luggage charge, admin-configurable surge multiplier
- **Trip history** per customer, with total spend and average fare
- **Trip cancellation** — cancels a customer's most recent active trip; cancelled trips are excluded from totals but kept in the log
- **Fare comparison** between any two vehicles for a given distance (via a `friend` function)
- **Lambda-based filtering** of trips above a fare threshold
- **Customer merging** via overloaded `operator+`, combining two customers' trip histories
- **Search** trips by (partial, case-insensitive) customer name
- **Fleet statistics**: trips per vehicle, earnings per vehicle, most popular vehicle, average fare
- **File persistence**: every trip is appended to `trip_history.txt`; the admin can export a full CSV summary to `trip_summary.csv`
- **Admin panel** (password protected) for fleet/earnings/customer stats, surge control, and exports
- Robust input handling and custom exceptions for invalid distances, invalid input, and invalid coupons

## Requirements

- A C++17-capable compiler (e.g. `g++` 7+ or `clang++`)
- No external libraries — only the C++ standard library

## Building

```bash
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -o smartfare smart_vehicle_fare_system.cpp
```

## Running

```bash
./smartfare
```

The program runs an interactive text menu; just follow the prompts.

## Main Menu

| # | Option |
|---|--------|
| 1 | Register / switch customer |
| 2 | Book a ride |
| 3 | View available vehicles |
| 4 | My trip history |
| 5 | Compare two vehicle fares (friend function) |
| 6 | Filter trips by fare (lambda) |
| 7 | Merge two customers (operator `+`) |
| 8 | Admin panel |
| 9 | Cancel my last trip |
| 10 | Search trips by customer name |
| 11 | Show fleet statistics |
| 12 | Exit |

## Admin Panel

Default password: **`admin123`**

| # | Option |
|---|--------|
| 1 | Total vehicles created |
| 2 | Total earnings |
| 3 | Total customers |
| 4 | View all trip records (from file) |
| 5 | Set surge multiplier |
| 6 | Export trip summary to CSV |
| 7 | Exit admin |

## Vehicle Fare Rules

| Vehicle | Base Rate | Min Fare | Slab Logic |
|---|---|---|---|
| Car | Rs.15/km | Rs.80 | 0–5 km: min fare · 5–15 km: Rs.15/km · 15+ km: Rs.12/km |
| Bus | Rs.5/km | Rs.30 | 0–10 km: min fare · 10+ km: Rs.5/km |
| Bike | Rs.8/km | Rs.40 | 0–3 km: min fare · 3+ km: Rs.8/km |
| Auto | Rs.10/km | Rs.50 | 0–4 km: min fare · 4+ km: Rs.10/km |
| Luxury Car | Rs.25/km | Rs.200 | Flat base + per-km, no slabs |
| Truck | Rs.18/km | Rs.150 | 0–8 km: min fare · 8+ km: Rs.18/km |
| Shared Cab | Rs.7/km | Rs.45 | 0–6 km: min fare · 6+ km: Rs.7/km, then 15% pooled discount |

Discounts (customer type + coupon) apply after surcharges, capped at 50% total.

## Output Files

- `trip_history.txt` — plain-text append log of every booked trip (created/updated automatically)
- `trip_summary.csv` — CSV export of all trips, generated on demand from the Admin Panel

## Project Structure (single file)

- **Exceptions**: `InvalidDistanceException`, `InvalidInputException`, `InvalidCouponException`
- **`Vehicle`** (abstract base) → `Car`, `Bus`, `Bike`, `Auto`, `LuxuryCar`, `Truck`, `SharedCab`
- **`Customer`** — profile, coupon, trip history, merge operator
- **`FareCalculator`** — surcharges, discounts, surge pricing
- **`FileHandler`** — trip logging and CSV export
- **`ReceiptGenerator`** — formatted receipt printing
- **`AdminPanel`** — password-gated admin operations
- Free functions: `compareFares` (friend), `currentTime`, `safeIntInput`, `safeDoubleInput`, `searchTripsByCustomer`, `showStatistics`
